          <span class="gradient-text">grounded answers.</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          Change the document, chunk size, retrieval count, and question.
          The simulator reveals what happens at every stage of the pipeline.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="concept-card">
        <h3>What RAG does</h3>
        <p>
          RAG gives a language model relevant information before it writes an
          answer. It is similar to letting someone consult notes before answering.
        </p>
        <div class="formula">
          Documents → Chunks → Vectors<br>
          Question → Retrieval → Context<br>
          Context + Question → Answer
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <nav class="pipeline" id="pipeline"></nav>

    <section class="workspace">
      <aside class="panel">
        <div class="panel-header">
          <div>
            <h3>Experiment controls</h3>
            <p>Modify the inputs, then run the pipeline.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="badge">No API needed</span>
        </div>

        <label for="documentInput">Knowledge document</label>
        <textarea id="documentInput"></textarea>

        <div class="control-grid">
          <div>
            <label for="chunkSize">Chunk size in words</label>
            <input id="chunkSize" type="number" min="12" max="100" value="35">
          </div>

          <div>
            <label for="topK">Chunks to retrieve</label>
            <select id="topK">
              <option value="1">1 chunk</option>
              <option value="2" selected>2 chunks</option>
              <option value="3">3 chunks</option>
              <option value="4">4 chunks</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>

        <label for="questionInput">Your question</label>
        <input
          id="questionInput"
          value="Why does chunk overlap help retrieval?"
        >

        <div class="button-row">
          <button class="primary-button" id="runButton">
            Run RAG pipeline
          </button>
          <button class="secondary-button" id="resetButton">
            Reset
          </button>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <section class="panel stage" aria-live="polite">
        <div class="stage-title">
          <h2 id="stageHeading"></h2>
          <p id="stageDescription"></p>
        </div>

        <div id="stageContent"></div>
      </section>
